The tools page is the developer edition's tools page — without a name list in it
==============================================================================

Skills come first, the section is grouped by the manifest's `owner` into three libraries with a
catch-all, and names are masked on the way to the screen — the card titles, the descriptions, the text
the search matches, and the reader, where a whole file used to arrive unredacted.

The map itself is NOT in this file. A name list is a list of the people it hides, and this file is
published, so shipping the patterns would hand out exactly what the redaction exists to hide. What ships
is an empty map with the shape documented; the machine that has names to hide supplies them at package
time from a file that is never committed:

    QUIXI_REDACT_NAMES=~/.config/quixidesk/redact-names.js makepkg -f

Each line of that file is one `[/pattern/gi, "replacement"],` entry. Without it the map is empty and the
page shows the library as it is — which is right for everyone whose library is their own.

`Max` is deliberately not in any map: it is a first name and also `Max: 250` and `Max width: 60`, and the
reader redacts file bodies, so mapping it turns working instructions into nonsense.

